-- Unit: the sort with exactly one value, spelled `()` — the empty tuple literal
-- (spec §4.5, `TupleLiteral ::= '(' ')'`).
-- There is NO bare `unit` keyword: writing `unit` in term position is a load error
-- ("expected resolved name, got unresolved"). Adding one would need a grammar
-- keyword and a Rust literal variant, neither of which exists.
sort anthill.prelude.Unit = ?
